&lt;p&gt;Warp is seeking a results-oriented Senior Product Marketing Manager, Enterprise to own how we bring Warp to engineering organizations. As software development shifts from interactive coding agents to cloud software factories, you will define how Warp wins the enterprise: shaping the narrative for VPs of Engineering and platform teams, building the assets that move deals, and turning bottoms-up developer adoption into company-wide deployments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will craft messaging and positioning for a technical buying committee, arm Sales with the tools to win competitive evaluations, and work closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, and Growth. This role is ideal for a strategic thinker who can hold both audiences at once: the developer who adopts Warp on their own, and the engineering leader who standardizes on it. You are a storyteller with deep empathy for developers, you are data informed, and you thrive in a fast-paced startup environment. This role reports to the Head of Growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Enterprise Positioning and Messaging:&lt;/strong&gt; Craft the narrative for how Warp delivers measurable ROI, security, and compliance to engineering organizations, differentiating us in a fast-consolidating market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the Sales Narrative and Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop the pitch, competitive battlecards, objection handling, and technical content that Sales uses to win evaluations against IDE-first and agent-native competitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Enterprise Launches:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product to shape the enterprise roadmap and lead go-to-market for features that unlock larger deployments, from security and admin controls to multi-agent orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Convert Bottoms-Up to Top-Down:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Growth and Sales to turn individual developer adoption into enterprise expansion, defining the signals and motions that move accounts from a handful of users to a company-wide standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Competitive and Buyer Research:&lt;/strong&gt; Run win/loss analysis, customer and prospect interviews, and competitive intelligence. Bring the voice of the engineering leader into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Proof:&lt;/strong&gt; Build the case studies, benchmarks, and ROI evidence that engineering leaders need to justify the decision internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of B2B product marketing experience, with meaningful time marketing to enterprise engineering organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience marketing to a technical buying committee: developers, engineering managers, VPs of Engineering, platform and security teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record building sales enablement that Sales actually uses, including competitive positioning in crowded markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work across both highly technical and highly creative teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience in data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex, high impact product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep product intuition and demonstrated ability to uncover insights and latent user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating in cross-functional teams, ideally in a fast-paced startup or high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a passion for learning more about the terminal and developer tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to roll up your sleeves to do all things necessary to make an early-stage startup successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developer tools, infrastructure, or related industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience coding or a technical background&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a bottoms-up or product-led motion that expanded into enterprise deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise security and compliance requirements in developer tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Warp operates from a place of high trust and transparency around compensation. We state the pay range that best aligns with our understanding of the market and the needs for the open role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When we find the right person, we try to put our best foot forward with an offer that excites you. We consider your skills, the level of experience you bring, and what similar jobs in the market pay, all while ensuring equal pay for equal work at Warp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total compensation at Warp consists of: (1) a market-competitive base salary, (2) a generous benefits package, and (3) meaningful equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The budgeted compensation amount for this role is targeted at &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FILL IN $170,000-200,000 BLANK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Exact compensation will vary based on skills and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to salary, all employees receive further compensation in the form of equity in the company. This is a meaningful stock option grant with a four-year vesting period and one-year cliff. Your equity is where most of the significant upside potential is. Comparing startup equity is always a bit tricky, so we’re happy to walk you through different valuation scenarios at the offer stage in order to help paint a clearer picture of the upside.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary, generous benefits, and meaningful equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% coverage on medical, dental, and vision benefits for employees (80% coverage for dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible remote-first culture, with optional office spaces in NYC and SF for folks who want to work together IRL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax FSA and Health Savings Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax Commuter Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 company holidays, 20 days of Paid Time Off, and unlimited sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;16 weeks of paid Parental Leave for both birthing and non-birthing parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Twice-a-year all company retreats in awesome locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A monthly gym and internet stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company-sponsored 401(k) through Vestwell&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A complimentary OneMedical membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Individuals seeking employment at Warp are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Warp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a company run by product-first builders, building a core product for all developers. We are committed to understanding our users deeply. We will ultimately build the best product and business if that team includes developers and designers from a wide range of backgrounds. The early team comes from Google, Dropbox, Gem, LinkedIn, and Facebook. We are looking for passionate individuals to join us and help bring Warp to the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We value honesty, humility, and pragmatism, and our core product principle is focusing on the user. If you’re interested in learning more about our company values and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;the culture of our engineering team, please take a look at our internal&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://warp.dev/how-we-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&#39;How We Work&#39;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;guide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re very fortunate to be backed by a great group of venture capital firms. In August 2023, we announced a $50M Series B funding round ($73M total raised), led by Sequoia Capital.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our other investors include Google Ventures, Neo, and Box Group. We are also backed by a network of passionate angels, including Dylan Field (Co-Founder and CEO,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/why-im-leading-warps-series-dylan-field/&quot;&gt;Figma&lt;/a&gt;), Elad Gil (early investor in Airbnb, Pinterest, Stripe, and Square), Jeff Weiner (Executive Chairman and Ex-CEO, LinkedIn), Marc Benioff (Founder and CEO, Salesforce), and Sam Altman (Co-Founder &amp;amp; CEO, OpenAI).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
